key sanctions on Eritrea as Houthi attacks disrupt Red Sea shipping and fighting escalates in Ethiopia's Tigray region. Analysts say Eritrea's strategic value is growing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UNGA Day 4: Lebanese on deck after defiant Netanyahu speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:690c4ee7aeac6543fda1e279a792f8fd5acaaaa9f6155b1d78fa581e511c2ab1</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/unga-day-4-lebanese-on-deck-after-defiant-netanyahu-speech/live-79366211--b41d71904bbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/unga-day-4-lebanese-on-deck-after-defiant-netanyahu-speech/live-79366211?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A day after a divisive speech by Israeli Prime Minister Netanyahu, the prime minister of Lebanon will address the UN General Assembly. Leaders from Pakistan and Iraq are also set to speak on the meeting's 4th day.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>A HRW report shows how South Korean women face systemic barriers to climbing the career ladder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea74da4e9bc5dece819f5b858fb00d607a051154d2b5d8a2750fcf89de133ed2</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-hrw-report-shows-how-south-korean-women-face-systemic-barriers-to-climbing-the-career-ladder/a-79431285--df02030583ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-hrw-report-shows-how-south-korean-women-face-systemic-barriers-to-climbing-the-career-ladder/a-79431285?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report shows how in South Korea, women on average earn less and have fewer employment opportunities throughout their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Bulgaria become a global leader in battery storage and what this means for the country's grid and energy market?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eef60d75af21ae8bd0340cbbb0bcbcd7c5504e1ef45e95b70c0c0dc0055cdbc2</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-bulgaria-become-a-global-leader-in-battery-storage-and-what-this-means-for-the-country-s-grid-an/a-79428289--917b8ba9c523.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-bulgaria-become-a-global-leader-in-battery-storage-and-what-this-means-for-the-country-s-grid-and-energy-market/a-79428289?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In under two years, Bulgaria has become one of the world's most battery-intensive energy markets. Can the surge last — and what will it mean for conventional power generators?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian President Pezeshkian brought a diplomatic tone to New York for UNGA. What did his remarks signal?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8027eebd490d931726cdefc8b52e311e3471f2f217f270e7bfcecd97f71da0e3</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-president-pezeshkian-brought-a-diplomatic-tone-to-new-york-for-unga-what-did-his-remarks-sig/a-79428890--b543693f4fe7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-president-pezeshkian-brought-a-diplomatic-tone-to-new-york-for-unga-what-did-his-remarks-signal/a-79428890?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran's president used his trip to New York this week for the UN General Assembly to signal openness to talks over the nuclear dispute. However, the chances of a major breakthrough on the war remain low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>After Xi-Trump summit, US-China rivalry remains frozen. Is this to Beijing's advantage?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f125e428a155e019918a0898189036403c9e147c4665be413d8ea69ec8a46f2</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-xi-trump-summit-us-china-rivalry-remains-frozen-is-this-to-beijing-s-advantage/a-79427127--110c4fa9d052.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-xi-trump-summit-us-china-rivalry-remains-frozen-is-this-to-beijing-s-advantage/a-79427127?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president showcased White House construction projects and hosted a lavish dinner with tech CEOs, but the summit made little progress on key issues such as trade tensions and AI regulation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV begins four-day pilgrimage to France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a76a9f067a9a3734c3bcb8505c8583102d43cd04d7c3846dbf220d1ffde60b3</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T10:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-begins-four-day-pilgrimage-to-france/a-79428252--49d1e7a0a624.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-begins-four-day-pilgrimage-to-france/a-79428252?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pope has landed in Paris, where he and President Macron will navigate the rules of religious state visits in secular France. Leo's trip will mix pilgrimage and politics on questions of morality and human existence.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen, Audi to recall almost 1 million cars in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:755d2ba0ee5fa926788e59fb28b477d47906e51841b06a7f4075682846f21a0d</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-audi-to-recall-almost-1-million-cars-in-germany/a-79426960--b707dbde3045.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-audi-to-recall-almost-1-million-cars-in-germany/a-79426960?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Volkswagen and its subsidiary Audi are to recall nearly a million vehicles in Germany due to a potential steering fault.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why farmers are pairing crops with solar panels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc55fd6d221118fc60a690ffb9aa0dbbe0351a4ee4fb78cacbf68081428912a8</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T09:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-farmers-are-pairing-crops-with-solar-panels/a-79233970--008efaae1ed6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-farmers-are-pairing-crops-with-solar-panels/a-79233970?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From cooler soil to paid grazing land, farmers are finding solar panels can do more than generate power.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Elections 'rigged,' allege Rahul Gandhi and Cockroach party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1383048fc360887b8fa1999f306c0a7369823b46aa26a4ff9296ca21dbbb4335</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T08:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-elections-rigged-allege-rahul-gandhi-and-cockroach-party/live-79422469--d3f07cf19359.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-elections-rigged-allege-rahul-gandhi-and-cockroach-party/live-79422469?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Cockroach party has urged India's opposition parties to stop contesting what it calls "rigged" elections and threatened nationwide protests over the Election Commission's voter-list revision. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parliament approves fuel tax cut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:495b0262215403271f61e3e0c9060556b98f641b13c8c2c8edacba43d10bea61</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T08:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-approves-fuel-tax-cut/live-79424882--bd35c461e842.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-approves-fuel-tax-cut/live-79424882?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German lawmakers hope to drive down fuel prices by cutting taxes on gas and diesel from October 1. Meanwhile, students in many cities are set to protest against military conscription. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Italy to ban burqa in schools, limit foreign pupils</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ea6003c182f663d6546b301ab2d65fe922757b0bba046dfdd09015ceba648ed</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-to-ban-burqa-in-schools-limit-foreign-pupils/a-79423432--d459be98ca4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-to-ban-burqa-in-schools-limit-foreign-pupils/a-79423432?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni’s government has passed new school rules capping the number of students who don't speak fluent Italian and banning face coverings.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Internet disrupted in Tigray amid conflict escalation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f671b502f7fed8debf2d556a013cccbe512fb388aded62face5182ea0b46d07</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:58:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T07:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-internet-disrupted-in-tigray-amid-conflict-escalation/a-79424191--15879d4d7c53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-internet-disrupted-in-tigray-amid-conflict-escalation/a-79424191?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A web monitor reported an internet disruption in northern Ethiopia amid renewed fighting between the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) and the federal government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How renewed fighting in Tigray could spread across the Horn of Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59f9b3ef8dfa9b6be887f76ccaa29915fdbb3df29eb2895c73d3a451aba240ef</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:57:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-renewed-fighting-in-tigray-could-spread-across-the-horn-of-africa/a-79410333--a598375bf2c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-renewed-fighting-in-tigray-could-spread-across-the-horn-of-africa/a-79410333?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The fresh hostilities in Ethiopia's Tigray region come after months of growing animosity between rebel forces and the federal government. Horn of Africa expert Martin Plaut warns of possible regional spillover.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal's leader says his country is paying the price of climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:390f218412ca5b823e710703b23f76a00929f7bb4d94d2a8880a8d7fa57cbdcb</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:57:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T04:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-leader-says-his-country-is-paying-the-price-of-climate-change/a-79421807--a05a6077a529.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-leader-says-his-country-is-paying-the-price-of-climate-change/a-79421807?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepalese Prime Minister Balendra Shah called the devastating Nepal-Tibet floods a "warning to the world" — and questioned if the world had "really heard that warning."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jürgen Klopp starts Germany job with shaky Netherlands draw</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29144e96c631585fa1f6f6413b885b41c311b4688e5d7ef682be8cda46df9544</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:57:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T22:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/j_rgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143--fa995d928e4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jürgen-klopp-starts-germany-job-with-shaky-netherlands-draw/a-79420143?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A late Netherlands goal denied Jürgen Klopp a win in his first match as Germany coach. The former Liverpool and Borussia Dortmund boss has big ambitions, but the game showed he's going to need more time to achieve them.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:440679a12d1f2f49a3f404a9d657ce332bf9fa391717016c8df370dd53e1455e</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:57:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's military says it killed hundreds of TPLF rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0d6652bba73b0166fad7908173a5e9e6ca14c983159998ac9c077a995323cf0</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:57:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-military-says-it-killed-hundreds-of-tplf-rebels/a-79419173--d10c751c44c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-military-says-it-killed-hundreds-of-tplf-rebels/a-79419173?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TPLF fought against against the Ethiopian military from 2020 to 2022 in a conflict that saw hundreds of thousands of civilians killed. A resumption of fighting has sparked fears of another brutal war.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After several difficult years, economists now expect German economy to grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1e5e60ae31e6b290f8fbc3af3272fefe977f8cfa4a52615ca17eeb61856b806</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:57:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591--9a99d252976e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-several-difficult-years-economists-now-expect-german-economy-to-grow/a-79418591?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's economy is growing again, but recovery remains on shaky ground. High government spending is keeping the economy afloat, while energy prices, a shortage of skilled workers and debt continue to weigh on it.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW, Politico regain access to White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff0696af47a1728f45876ebb1331764a8b9caaca1b70c4beb42fdb601a1bcbe</id><updated>2026-09-25T13:57:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-politico-regain-access-to-white-house/a-79405693--d2a4fb75d5c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-politico-regain-access-to-white-house/a-79405693?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A federal judge has ordered President Trump to restore White House access to CNN, MS NOW and Politico after he banned the media outlets from the premises. Hours later, the media announced they had been granted access.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
